NNAAMMEE
     sseettffiibb — execute a utility with an altered default network view

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     sseettffiibb [--FF] _f_i_b _u_t_i_l_i_t_y [_a_r_g_u_m_e_n_t _._._.]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The sseettffiibb utility runs another _u_t_i_l_i_t_y with a different routing table.
     The table number _f_i_b will be used by default for all sockets started by
     this process or descendants.

EENNVVIIRROONNMMEENNTT
     The PATH environment variable is used to locate the requested _u_t_i_l_i_t_y if
     the name contains no ‘/’ characters.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     If _u_t_i_l_i_t_y is invoked, the exit status of sseettffiibb is the exit status of
     _u_t_i_l_i_t_y.

     An exit status of 126 indicates _u_t_i_l_i_t_y was found, but could not be exe‐
     cuted.  An exit status of 127 indicates _u_t_i_l_i_t_y could not be found.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     Run netstat(1) to view the second routing table.

           setfib -F 1 netstat -rn
     or
           setfib 1 netstat -rn
     or
           setfib -1 netstat -rn

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     setfib(2), setsockopt(2)

SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The sseettffiibb utility is a FreeBSD specific extension.  However, many
     UNIX-like systems have an equivalent function.

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The sseettffiibb utility appeared in FreeBSD 7.1.

